''Docker Commands and Operations''

* How does one build a Docker image?
** With <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker build">docker build</$button> -t tagname ., where . refers to the directory containing the Dockerfile.
* What command would you use to run a Docker container?
** <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker run">docker run</$button> [OPTIONS] IMAGE [COMMAND] [ARG...]. For example, docker run -it ubuntu bash starts an interactive session with an Ubuntu container.
* How do you manage Docker containers?
** Key commands include:
*** <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker ps">docker ps</$button> for listing running containers
*** <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker stop">docker stop</$button> CONTAINER_ID for stopping a container
*** <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker rm">docker rm</$button> CONTAINER_ID for removing a container
*** <$button message="tm-modal" param="docker start">docker start</$button> CONTAINER_ID to start a stopped container

* What is Docker Compose, and why might you use it?
** <$button message="tm-modal" param="Docker Compose">Docker Compose</$button> is a tool for defining and running multi-container Docker applications. It uses a YAML file to configure application’s services, networks, and volumes. It simplifies development, testing, and deployment of multi-container applications.